§ 2° If the convicted person has repaired the damage,

except when impossible to do so, and if the circumstances of art. 59 of this Code are entirely favorable to him, the judge may replace the requirement of the previous paragraph with the following conditions, applied cumulatively:
(Wording given by Law No. 9,268 of April 1, 1996)
a) prohibition from frequenting certain places;
(Wording given by Law No. 7,209 of July 11, 1984)
b) prohibition from leaving the district where he resides, without authorization from the judge;
(Wording given by Law No. 7,209 of July 11, 1984)
c) personal and mandatory appearance in court, monthly, to inform and justify his activities.
(Wording given by Law No. 7,209 of July 11, 1984)

